WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.159 --> 00:00:04.229
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar and you're watching Mind Your Decisions.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:11.700
It was the problem that left some of the smartest math students in the state stumped and was...

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:19.770
described as one of the hardest problems they ever encountered, reports Pallavi Singhal in The Sydney Morning Herald.

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:25.079
This problem was given to 17 year old students in Australia.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:30.209
I tried it and honestly, I would not have solved it in an exam.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:36.809
I benefited from a video explanation by Phillip Liang who was the top student in the state.

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:41.969
I encourage you to check out the video and there's a clickable link in the video description.

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:44.969
So what was the problem in?

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:47.289
Triangle ABC

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:52.709
Point D is chosen on side AB and point E is chosen on side AC

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:56.159
So that DE is parallel to BC and BC

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:00.209
Divided by DE is equal to the square root of two.

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:04.169
The process is repeated two more times.

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:10.109
Point F is chosen on side BC and point G is chosen on side BA

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:17.159
So that FG is parallel to CA and CA divided by FG is equal to the square root of two.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:25.829
Point H is chosen on side CB and point A is chosen on side CA so that HI is

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.320
Parallel to BA and BA divided by HI is equal to the square root of two.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.699
The segment's FG and HI intersect at X,

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:43.049
DE and HI intersect at Yand DE and FG intersect at Z.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.890
There are two parts of this question...

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.950
First

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.909
Prove that DY is equal to ZE and

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.909
Second, find the exact value of the ratio YZ divided by BC

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:04.290
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready, keep watching the video for a solution.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.710
So let's get started with the diagram. We need to prove that DY is equal to ZE

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:34.790
Now one of the reasons this problem is complicated is because it's a little bit of an alphabet soup.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:42.709
So one of the benefits of making a video is that I can focus on just the parts that matter for any particular step.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.969
So let's get started by focusing just on these two triangles.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:54.290
The first thing I will claim is a triangle BFG is similar to triangle BCA.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.809
This is because both triangles share the common angle B.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:07.279
Their other angles are equal because they are corresponding angles of parallel lines GF || AC.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:15.139
Next, we have that BC divided by BF is equal to the square root of 2.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.420
This is because the triangles are similar and it's given that AC

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.540
divided by GF is equal to the square root of 2

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.300
Now we're going to do the same sort of thing with another set of triangles

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:35.570
Here we have the triangle CHI is similar to triangle CBA.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.160
Why is that?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:46.040
Well, they share a common angle C and the other angles are equal because HI and AB are given to be parallel.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:56.269
So we now can conclude that BC divided by HC is equal to the square root of 2. That's because the triangles are similar and...

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.120
We were given that BA divided by HI is equal to the square root of 2.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.890
So what can we do with this?

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:09.110
Well, we have two different fractions that are equal to the square root of 2, so they must be equal to each other.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.339
Furthermore, their numerators are both BC.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.419
This means their denominators must also be equal. So we have HC is equal to BF.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.710
Now we're going to go back to our original diagram.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.170
The next thing to notice is that this shape, DYHB is a parallelogram.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.559
That's because the opposite sides are given to be parallel from the given information.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:47.719
We will also have that ZECF is a parallelogram for the same sort of reason.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:55.520
So now we start out that DY is equal to BH because they're opposite sides of a parallelogram.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.550
Then BH is equal to BC - HC.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:07.790
We just proved that BF is equal to HC, so this is equal to BC minus BF.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.780
but BC minus BF is equal to FC.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:16.670
And then FC is equal to ZE because they're opposite sides of a parallelogram.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.739
So we've proven that DY is equal to ZE and we're done with the first part of this question.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.589
Now, let's go to the second part of the question.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.049
We need to find the exact value of the ratio YZ divided by BC.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:36.619
So on a problem like this, it's not exactly clear how to approach it and how to get to the end result.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.070
So just start out with some information that you do know.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.480
Well, we do know that YZ is equal to DE minus DY minus ZE.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:55.040
We just proved that DY is equal to ZE so we can then say this is equal to DE minus 2 times ZE.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:01.610
Next ZE is equal to FC because we have opposite sides of a parallelogram.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:06.320
We'll then you replace FC with BC minus BF.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.640
We're getting closer to putting everything in terms of BC.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.080
Now recall that BF is equal to BC divided by the square root of 2.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:19.039
So we can substitute that in now.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.529
All we need to do is put DE in terms of BC.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:26.630
But that was also given information. DE is equal to BC divided by the square root of 2

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:32.330
So, we now factor out the BC and simplify and we get the following expression.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.279
We then just need to divide both sides by BC so that we get...

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:42.590
YZ divided by BC is equal to 3 minus 2 times the square root of 2 all over the square root of 2.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.440
And that's our answer.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.419
Did you figure it out?

